Today’s focus was on planning the dashboard structure before building the visualizations. Instead of immediately creating charts in Excel, I mapped out the visual components on paper to determine the most effective way to communicate insights from the HR dataset.

Planned Visualizations
	1.	Annual Salary by Department
	•	Chart Type: Bar Chart
	•	Axis: Department
	•	Values: Total Annual Salary
	2.	Compensation by Department
	•	Chart Type: Column Chart
	•	Axis: Department
	•	Values: Total Compensation
	3.	Average Salary by Gender
	•	Chart Type: Bar Chart
	•	Axis: Gender
	•	Values: Average Salary
	4.	Hiring Trend Over Time
	•	Chart Type: Line Chart
	•	Axis: Hire Year
	•	Values: Total Employees Hired
	5.	Employees Leaving by Year
	•	Chart Type: Line Chart
	•	Axis: Leave Year
	•	Values: Number of Employees Who Left

Key Takeaway

Planning the dashboard layout beforehand helps clarify which insights need to be communicated and which visualizations best support those insights. This approach ensures the dashboard is designed with a clear analytical objective rather than simply displaying data.